---
title: "Alma Analytics Catalog File Parser"
output: html_document
params:
  catalog_file: "data/Annual Stats FY 2025-2026.catalog"
  output_dir: "output"
---

## Run the pipeline

The user-facing wrapper is `choose_catalog_file_and_run_pipeline.R`. When used
interactively in RStudio, calling `run_catalog_pipeline()` without a path opens
a menu containing `.catalog` files from the repository's `data/` directory and
the user's `~/Downloads` directory.

This report supplies the `catalog_file` parameter explicitly instead of opening
that menu, which keeps the report reproducible when rendered from RStudio or the
command line.

```{r setup}
source("choose_catalog_file_and_run_pipeline.R")

catalog <- run_catalog_pipeline(
  catalog_path = params$catalog_file,
  output_dir = params$output_dir
)
```

To choose a file interactively in the RStudio Console instead, run:

```{r interactive-example, eval=FALSE}
source("choose_catalog_file_and_run_pipeline.R")
catalog <- run_catalog_pipeline()
```

## Catalog summary

```{r catalog-summary}
catalog[c(
  "catalog_index", "object_title", "object_kind", "xml_root_name",
  "closest_folder", "closest_level_object", "subject_area", "original_path"
)]
```

## Object counts

```{r object-counts}
as.data.frame(table(catalog$object_kind), stringsAsFactors = FALSE)
```

## Generated files

```{r generated-files}
data.frame(file = list.files(params$output_dir, full.names = TRUE))
```
